root.\n\nActually creating a commit requires a base ref for `origin/main`. I can create a branch `main` and a ref `origin/main` pointing at an initial commit of the unchanged baseline... but everything is \"changed\" relative to nothing. The ownership check would then flag all my touched files — which are exactly the declared touchedAreas. Actually that would PASS the ownership gate if all changed files are within ownedPaths. But many other files are identical, so diff against the initial commit shows only my new files. But git add -A would track everything; then committing 17k files creates the initial commit including my new files → diff empty.\n\nBetter: commit with my new files excluded? Complicated.\n\nI'll accept the structural validate as the runnable harness gate and clearly note the diff-backed run needs git metadata absent from this isolated trial workspace. That is truthful and matches \"report exact checks you actually ran.\"\n\nNow, let me also produce the S05-SHA256SUMS and finish remaining checks: typecheck (needs tsgo), lint (needs eslint), comms replay/compare (needs git rev-parse HEAD → will fail without git).\n\nLet me test comms:replay and comms:compare.\n\nActually comms replay requires git rev-parse HEAD. Without git it fails. Let me check.\n\nLet me run eslint on the touched test — eslint is installed in D:\\ClawX node_modules, and now exposed via the junction. Let's try.\n\nAnd typecheck:test needs tsgo. Let me check.\n\nLet me run these."}}
